  "english": "18. Sunday. Tone 4 [Dadz / DDz]. Fourth [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 6 [g3 / gyun]: \"Glorified Son\" (Paravorial vordi). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [g3 / gyun]: \"Awful\" (Ahagin) and \"You who are above\" (Or i verd es).\n24. Saturday. Tone 5 [Gadz / GDz]. David the Prophet, and James the Apostle.\n25. Sunday. Tone 6 [Gak / GK]. Fifth [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 6 [gk / gyun]: \"From eternity\" (Nakhahavitean). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [gk / gyun]: \"Taking our [likeness]\" (Areal ev mer), to the end.\n29. Thursday. Tone 2 [Ak / AK]. The Sons of Thunder. Barekendan of the Fast of the Nativity.\n31. Saturday. Tone 4 [Bk / BK]. Fast. Of the Patriarchs: Basil of Caesarea, and the others.\n\nJanuary\n1. Sunday. Tone 5 [Gadz / GDz]. Sixth [Sunday] of the Fast. Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [GDz]: \"Glorified is your\" (Paravorial e ko), to the end.\n2. Monday. Tone 6 [Gak / GK]. Fast. Canticle [Harts] Tone 8 [dk / dzyun]: \"God of our fathers, have mercy\" (Astvats hartsn merots voghormia).\n5. Thursday. Tone 1 [Adz / ADz]. Eve of the Nativity of Christ.\n[Roman weekly cycle index: 5]\nCanticle [Harts] Tone 2 [ak / ayp]: \"You who are exalted\" (Or bardzryald es).\n26. Tuesday. Tone 1 [Adz / ADz]. Tryphon, Parsamas, and Onuphrius the hermits.\n27. Wednesday. Tone 2 [Ak / AK]. Canticle [Harts] of Penitence: \"The children sang\" (Yergein mankunkn).\n28. Thursday. Tone 3 [Bdz / BDz]. Eugenius, Macarius, and the others. Canticle [Harts] Tone 2 [b]: \"Without malice\" (Anokhakal).\n30. Saturday. Tone 5 [Gadz / GDz]. Gregory the Theologian.\n31. Sunday. Tone 6 [Gak / GK]. Third [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 6 [gk / gyun]: \"Today He was sacrificed\" (Aysor zhenav). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [gk / gyun]: \"Vision of the lightning-like\" (Tesil paylaknadzev). For what lies below, see the First Volume after Transfiguration; but the canticles and tones you shall find here.\n\nFebruary\n1. Monday. Tone 7 [Ddz / DDz]. Cyprian the Bishop, and the others. Canticle [Harts] Tone 5 [b3 / pen]: \"With your saints\" (Ynd surbs ko).\n2. Tuesday. Tone 8 [Dk / DK]. Athenogenes the Bishop, and the others. Canticle [Harts] Tone 4 [bk / pen]: \"We bless you, Lord\" (Orhnemk zkyez Ter).\n3. Wednesday. Tone 1 [Adz / ADz]. Canticle [Harts] of Penitence Tone 2 [ak / ayp]: \"Glorified forever\" (Paravorial yavitian).\n4. Thursday. Tone 2 [Ak / AK]. The Forefathers: Adam, Abel, and the others.\n\nJanuary\n6. WEDNESDAY. Tone 5 [Gadz / GDz]. Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ. The meat-eating period (dispensation) is forty days.\n14. Thursday. Tone 7 [Ddz / DDz]. John the Forerunner (Precursor).\n16. Saturday. Tone 7 [Ddz / DDz]. Peter the Patriarch, Blaise, and the others.\n17. Sunday. Tone 8 [Dk / DK]. First [Sunday]. Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 8 [dk / dzyun]: \"The tree of the resurrection\" (Tsarots yarutean).\n18. Monday. Tone 1 [Adz / ADz]. Antony the Hermit.\n19. Tuesday. Tone 2 [Ak / AK]. Theodosius the King, and the Holy Infants of Ephesus.\n20. Wednesday. Tone 3 [Bdz / BDz]. Canticle [Harts] of Penitence Tone 8 [dk / dzyun]: \"God of our fathers\" (Astvats hartsn merots).\n21. Thursday. Tone 4 [Bk / BK]. Cyriacus and Julitta, and Gordius, Polyeuctus, and Grigoris. Canticle [Harts] Tone 2 [ak / ayp]: \"Holy God, Creator\" (Surb Astvats ararich).\n23. Saturday. Tone 6 [Gak / GK]. Athanasius and Cyril, Patriarchs.\n24. Sunday. Tone 7 [Ddz / DDz]. Second [Sunday]. Canticle [Harts] Tone 7 [d3 / dzyun]: \"Creator of creatures\" (Ararichd araratsots). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 7 [d3 / dzyun]: \"The resurrection of the Son of God\" (Zyarutiun Astvatsordvoyn).\n25. Monday. Tone 8 [Dk / DK]. Vahan of Goghtn, and Eugenie the Virgin, and the others.",
